CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ hidden friend not found for X: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ found for sentinel: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ friend template found by ADL: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A friend function template first declared in a class was entered into the
enclosing namespace and found by ordinary lookup for any arguments, so
`a == b' was valid for an unrelated class.  libc++'s unreachable_sentinel_t
has such an operator==, and evaluating it for an iterator during the
instantiation of iterator_traits<It> cached a wrong
__is_primary_template<iterator_traits<It>> ("already declared with
different type", cpp20_concept_iterator_chain on macOS).
